-- title:
--   Prime-to-p inertia differences lie in the toric part
-- statement:
--   Fix $N_0 \ge 1$ and a prime $p$ with $p \nmid N_0$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbf{Q}}$ with $p$ a non-unit in $A$ (so the residue field $\kappa = \mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ has characteristic $p$), a level datum $\Lambda$ of level $N_0$ at $p$ over $A$ satisfying `IsJacobian` (its structure map is an abelian-scheme bundle, its relative group law is commutative, the dictionaries `pts`, `ptsSp` are additive, Galois-equivariant and compatible with reduction, and every Hecke element is realised by an endomorphism over the base), and an object $O$ of `JZeroNeronObjectAtP N₀ p hpN₀ A hA Λ`, with its group scheme $O.G$ over the base, its bijection $O.\mathrm{pts}$ between $\mathrm{JZero}(N_0p) = \mathrm{Pic}^0$ of the base-changed full modular function field of level $N_0p$ and the generic points of $O.g$, its special-fibre torus $O.\mathrm{torusFibre}$ of rank $O.\mathrm{toricRank}$, its supersingular finite set $O.\mathrm{ssFinset}$ of places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,\kappa\,N_0$, and its Frobenius $O.\mathrm{frob}$. Assume further given: modular polynomial data for $p$ satisfying the Kronecker congruence; integrality of the two degeneracy embeddings $\alpha,\beta$ at level $(N_0,p)$; a place specialization $P$ of level $N_0$ at $A$ with reduction map $\mathrm{residue}\,A$ to $\kappa$; a prolongation tuple $Rt$ for $P$ satisfying `IsModel`, the regularity law, the node-value law at $O.\mathrm{ssFinset}$ and the fixed-place order law; the identification $O.\mathrm{frob} = \mathrm{arithFrobC}\,p\,\kappa\,N_0$; an additive map $\mathrm{sp}$ from the $I_A$-invariants of $\mathrm{JZero}(N_0p)$, where $I_A$ is the image of the inertia subgroup of $A$ over $\mathbf{Q}$ in $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbf{Q}}/\mathbf{Q})$, to the glued $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ over $\kappa$ for the node set $\mathrm{nodePairsOfPlaces}$ of $\mathrm{arithFrobC}\,p\,\kappa\,N_0$ on $O.\mathrm{ssFinset}$, which is a glued specialization for $P$ (it sends the class of a good degree-zero divisor to the class of its glue datum); the bridge hypothesis that an invariant class $x$ has $O.\mathrm{pts}\,x$ factoring through an $A$-point of $O.g$ if and only if $x$ is a good class for that node set; and the torus clause that, for an invariant $x$ and an $A$-point $s$ with $(O.\mathrm{pts}\,x)_1 = \mathrm{barPt}\,A \circ s_1$, the reduction of $s$ to the special fibre factors through $O.\mathrm{torusFibre}$ exactly when the image of $\mathrm{sp}\,x$ under $\mathrm{toPic0Pair}$ (the pair of divisor classes in $\mathrm{Pic}^0$) vanishes. The conclusion: for every $m$ coprime to $p$, every $\sigma \in I_A$ and every $m$-torsion class $x$ of $\mathrm{JZero}(N_0p)$, the difference $\sigma \cdot x - x$ lies in $O.\mathrm{toricPts}\,m$, the subgroup generated by the range of $O.\mathrm{toricPoint}\,m$ (trivial if $m = 0$).
--
--   This is the prime-to-$p$ half of Grothendieck's description of the action of inertia on the torsion of a semistable abelian variety — $(\sigma - 1)$ carries $m$-torsion into the toric part for $\sigma$ in inertia and $p \nmid m$ — here for a Néron object attached to $J_0(N_0p)$ at $p$, stated for an arbitrary such object once the glued-specialization bridge and the torus clause are assumed. It feeds the construction of a Néron object together with its bridge data in [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel.exists_jZeroNeronObjectAtP_and_bridge_representsRelSubPic_abqFibre_of_levelModel`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel.exists_jZeroNeronObjectAtP_and_bridge_representsRelSubPic_abqFibre_of_levelModel).
